<%#
  Structured data (JSON-LD) for search engines, written from an object.

  JSON.stringify writes every value as JSON: quotes, backslashes and line
  breaks escaped, numbers and booleans as they are. Every "<" is then written
  as \u003c, which a JSON reader reads as the same character, so no value can
  end this script element. Values are not HTML-escaped: a script element's
  text is never read for character references, so an "&#39;" there would
  reach search engines as those six characters instead of an apostrophe.

  Every JSON-LD block of the site is written through this partial; the Home
  tests hold the views to that.
-%>
<script type="application/ld+json">
<%- JSON.stringify(schema, null, 4).replace(/</g, '\\u003c') %>
</script>
